      "CVE": "CVE-2026-90949",
      "Description": "A flaw was found in GIMP's PSP (Paint Shop Pro) file loader. When processing a compressed selection channel, a heap-based buffer overflow can occur due to a mismatch between the allocated buffer size and the amount of data decompressed. A remote attacker could exploit this vulnerability by crafting a malicious PSP file. Opening this file in GIMP could lead to a crash or arbitrary code execution.",
      "Threats": [
        {
          "Type": "Impact",
          "Severity": "moderate"
        }
      ],
